[[- define "lore-entries.instructions" -]]
- Write an entry the owner asks for, drawn from the attached cards and the lorebook. Keep names, relationships, and facts consistent with them.
- One topic per entry: a person, place, faction, object, custom, or event.
- Title: a short title for the entry.
- Keys: 1 to 4 words or names a chat would use when the topic comes up, including common variants. Never a key an existing entry already has.
- Content: 1 to 3 short paragraphs in third person, present tense, stating facts the model needs to portray the topic. No dialogue, no {{user}} actions.
- Don't repeat what the existing entries already cover, including ones just written.
[[- end]]

[[- define "lore-entries.system" -]]
You write lorebook entries for roleplay. An entry is inserted into the chat's context when one of its keys appears in recent messages. Write one new entry.

